{"after":{"hasSentPipedInput":false,"statusMessage":"Waiting on model...","tokenUsage":{"maxAvailable":168000,"used":12523},"type":"confirming","updateState":"none"},"before":{"hasSentPipedInput":false,"statusMessage":"Waiting on model...","tokenUsage":{"maxAvailable":168000,"used":12523},"type":"confirming","updateState":"none"},"event":{"blocks":[{"data":[4,{"content":[{"run":{"progress":{},"result":{"absolutePath":"/Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/README.md","content":"1: # Flare vTPM Attestation\n2: \n3: Flare vTPM Attestation is a Solidity-based implementation designed to verify Virtual Trusted Platform Module (vTPM) quotes generated within Google Cloud Platform’s (GCP) Confidential Space. \n4: This solution enables the permissionless onboarding of multiple Trusted Execution Environments (TEEs) on Flare, establishing a verifiable chain of trust across the network.\n5: \n6: Verification cost: Approx. 2M gas\n7: \n8: ## Requirements\n9: \n10: - [Solidity](https://soliditylang.org) v0.8.27 or higher\n11: - [Foundry](https://getfoundry.sh)\n12: - [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (for example scripts)\n13: \n14: ## Usage\n15: \n16: Start by cloning the repository:\n17: \n18: ```bash\n19: git clone https://github.com/dineshpinto/flare-vtpm-attestation\n20: ```\n21: \n22: To compile the contracts, run:\n23: \n24: ```bash\n25: forge build\n26: ```\n27: \n28: To run the contract tests:\n29: \n30: ```bash\n31: forge test -vv\n32: ```\n33: \n34: - The `-vv` flag provides verbose output, useful for detailed test logging.\n35: - To generate a gas report for the contract functions, use the `--gas-report` flag.\n36: \n37: ### Deploying the contracts\n38: \n39: To deploy the contracts, you can use a Foundry script along with your preferred RPC URL and private key:\n40: \n41: ```bash\n42: forge script script/FlareVtpmAttestation.s.sol:FlareVtpmAttestationScript --rpc-url ${FLARE_RPC_URL} --private-key ${DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY}\n43: ```\n44: \n45: To maintain code consistency and adhere to Solidity style guidelines, format the code with:\n46: \n47: ```bash\n48: forge fmt\n49: ```\n50: \n51: # Python\n52: \n53: The example logic is already written out in Python. To run it:\n54: \n55: ```bash\n56: cd py/\n57: uv sync --all-extras\n58: ```\n59: \n60: Example attestation tokens are stored in `py/data/`, to test them:\n61: \n62: ```bash\n63: uv run pki_attestation_validation.py\n64: uv run oidc_attestation_validation.py\n65: ```\n66: \n67: Note these actual validation may fail as the attestation tokens may be outdated."},"status":"done","trackFiles":["file:///Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/README.md"]},"toolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_018fif6T1JdSr1uvs1UXMPyj","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"}],"type":"message"},{"data":[{"id":"toolu_vrtx_018fif6T1JdSr1uvs1UXMPyj","input":{"path":"README.md"},"name":"Read","type":"tool_use"},{"run":{"progress":{},"result":{"absolutePath":"/Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/README.md","content":"1: # Flare vTPM Attestation\n2: \n3: Flare vTPM Attestation is a Solidity-based implementation designed to verify Virtual Trusted Platform Module (vTPM) quotes generated within Google Cloud Platform’s (GCP) Confidential Space. \n4: This solution enables the permissionless onboarding of multiple Trusted Execution Environments (TEEs) on Flare, establishing a verifiable chain of trust across the network.\n5: \n6: Verification cost: Approx. 2M gas\n7: \n8: ## Requirements\n9: \n10: - [Solidity](https://soliditylang.org) v0.8.27 or higher\n11: - [Foundry](https://getfoundry.sh)\n12: - [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (for example scripts)\n13: \n14: ## Usage\n15: \n16: Start by cloning the repository:\n17: \n18: ```bash\n19: git clone https://github.com/dineshpinto/flare-vtpm-attestation\n20: ```\n21: \n22: To compile the contracts, run:\n23: \n24: ```bash\n25: forge build\n26: ```\n27: \n28: To run the contract tests:\n29: \n30: ```bash\n31: forge test -vv\n32: ```\n33: \n34: - The `-vv` flag provides verbose output, useful for detailed test logging.\n35: - To generate a gas report for the contract functions, use the `--gas-report` flag.\n36: \n37: ### Deploying the contracts\n38: \n39: To deploy the contracts, you can use a Foundry script along with your preferred RPC URL and private key:\n40: \n41: ```bash\n42: forge script script/FlareVtpmAttestation.s.sol:FlareVtpmAttestationScript --rpc-url ${FLARE_RPC_URL} --private-key ${DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY}\n43: ```\n44: \n45: To maintain code consistency and adhere to Solidity style guidelines, format the code with:\n46: \n47: ```bash\n48: forge fmt\n49: ```\n50: \n51: # Python\n52: \n53: The example logic is already written out in Python. To run it:\n54: \n55: ```bash\n56: cd py/\n57: uv sync --all-extras\n58: ```\n59: \n60: Example attestation tokens are stored in `py/data/`, to test them:\n61: \n62: ```bash\n63: uv run pki_attestation_validation.py\n64: uv run oidc_attestation_validation.py\n65: ```\n66: \n67: Note these actual validation may fail as the attestation tokens may be outdated."},"status":"done","trackFiles":["file:///Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/README.md"]},"toolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_018fif6T1JdSr1uvs1UXMPyj","type":"tool_result"}],"type":"toolResult"}],"type":"messages"},"level":"debug","message":"Transition","name":"terminal","timestamp":"2025-07-23T09:19:17.850Z"}
