tTokens":13222}},{"content":[{"run":{"progress":{},"result":{"absolutePath":"/Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/README.md","content":"1: # Flare vTPM Attestation\n2: \n3: Flare vTPM Attestation is a Solidity-based implementation designed to verify Virtual Trusted Platform Module (vTPM) quotes generated within Google Cloud Platform’s (GCP) Confidential Space. \n4: This solution enables the permissionless onboarding of multiple Trusted Execution Environments (TEEs) on Flare, establishing a verifiable chain of trust across the network.\n5: \n6: Verification cost: Approx. 2M gas\n7: \n8: ## Requirements\n9: \n10: - [Solidity](https://soliditylang.org) v0.8.27 or higher\n11: - [Foundry](https://getfoundry.sh)\n12: - [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (for example scripts)\n13: \n14: ## Usage\n15: \n16: Start by cloning the repository:\n17: \n18: ```bash\n19: git clone https://github.com/dineshpinto/flare-vtpm-attestation\n20: ```\n21: \n22: To compile the contracts, run:\n23: \n24: ```bash\n25: forge build\n26: ```\n27: \n28: To run the contract tests:\n29: \n30: ```bash\n31: forge test -vv\n32: ```\n33: \n34: - The `-vv` flag provides verbose output, useful for detailed test logging.\n35: - To generate a gas report for the contract functions, use the `--gas-report` flag.\n36: \n37: ### Deploying the contracts\n38: \n39: To deploy the contracts, you can use a Foundry script along with your preferred RPC URL and private key:\n40: \n41: ```bash\n42: forge script script/FlareVtpmAttestation.s.sol:FlareVtpmAttestationScript --rpc-url ${FLARE_RPC_URL} --private-key ${DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY}\n43: ```\n44: \n45: To maintain code consistency and adhere to Solidity style guidelines, format the code with:\n46: \n47: ```bash\n48: forge fmt\n49: ```\n50: \n51: # Python\n52: \n53: The example logic is already written out in Python. To run it:\n54: \n55: ```bash\n56: cd py/\n57: uv sync --all-extras\n58: ```\n59: \n60: Example attestation tokens are stored in `py/data/`, to test them:\n61: \n62: ```bash\n63: uv run pki_attestation_validation.py\n64: uv run oidc_attestation_validation.py\n65: ```\n66: \n67: Note these actual validation may fail as the attestation tokens may be outdated."},"status":"done","trackFiles":["file:///Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/README.md"]},"toolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_018fif6T1JdSr1uvs1UXMPyj","type":"tool_result"},{"run":{"progress":{},"result":{"absolutePath":"/Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/foundry.toml","content":"1: [profile.default]\n2: src = \"contracts\"\n3: out = \"out\"\n4: libs = [\"lib\"]\n5: evm_version = \"london\"\n6: solc = \"0.8.27\"\n7: optimizer = true\n8: optimizer_runs = 200\n9: block_gas_limit = 15000000\n10: verbosity=2\n11: \n12: [rpc_endpoints]\n13: flare = \"${FLARE_RPC_URL}\"\n14: coston2 = \"${COSTON2_RPC_URL}\"\n15: \n16: [etherscan]\n17: flare = { key = \"${FLARESCAN_API_KEY}\", chain = 14, url = \"${FLARE_FLARESCAN_URL}\" }\n18: coston2 = { key = \"${FLARESCAN_API_KEY}\", chain = 114, url = \"${COSTON2_FLARESCAN_URL}\" }\n19: \n20: [fmt]\n21: sort_imports=true"},"status":"done","trackFiles":["file:///Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/foundry.toml"]},"toolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_01QW5HHBXFbenDJJHEZDnxLM","type":"tool_result"},{"run":{"error":{"absolutePath":"/Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/package.json","message":"File not found: file:///Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/package.json"},"status":"error"},"toolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_012GfcY2RVbAfGek94tD5UB3","type":"tool_result"},{"run":{"result":["FlareVtpmAttestation.sol","interfaces/","types/","utils/","verifiers/"],"status":"done"},"toolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_019knN6BD3X3u8aN37uyfWWj","type":"tool_result"},{"run":{"result":["FlareVtpmAttestation.t.sol"],"status":"done"},"toolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_01BfVZiWKShUUfi3UWLfaisk","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[{"id":"toolu_vrtx_01H9R1rMEaYrFTH5CUo2Sz1s","input":{"path":"py/pyproject.toml"},"name":"Read","type":"tool_use"},{"id":"toolu_vrtx_01NnqJPTQMzrafpGXbx53oV1","input":{"path":"py"},"name":"list_directory","type":"tool_use"},{"id":"toolu_vrtx_014t6eZAqMaVudYjFMK39xJf","input":{"path":"contracts/interfaces"},"name":"list_directory","type":"tool_use"},{"id":"toolu_vrtx_01Af8RAvA83Vjd1kQZeRXzgZ","input":{"path":"contracts/FlareVtpmAttestation.sol","read_range":[1,50]},"name":"Read","type":"tool_use"},{"id":"toolu_vrtx_01B4EwGghiuQazcQWYtZFuYA","input":{"path":"test/FlareVtpmAttestation.t.sol","read_range":[1,30]},"name":"Read","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant","state":{"stopReason":"tool_use","type":"complete"},"usage":{"cacheCreationInputTokens":1438,"cacheReadInputTokens":13214,"inputTokens":8,"maxInputTokens":168000,"outputTokens":271,"thinkingBudget":4000,"totalInputTokens":14660}},{"content":[{"run":{"progress":{},"result":{"absolutePath":"/Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/py/pyproject.toml","content":"1: [project]\n2: name = \"py\"\n3: version = \"0.1.0\"\n4: description = \"Add your description here\"\n5: readme = \"README.md\"\n6: authors = [\n7:   {name = \"Dinesh Pinto\", email = \"annual.fallout_0z@icloud.com\"},\n8: ]\n9: requires-python = \">=3.12\"\n10: dependencies = [\n11:     \"cryptography>=43.0.3\",\n12:     \"pyjwt>=2.9.0\",\n13:     \"pyopenssl>=24.2.1\",\n14:     \"requests>=2.32.3\",\n15:     \"web3>=7.4.0\",\n16: ]\n17: \n18: [dependency-groups]\n19: dev = [\n20:     \"pyright>=1.1.387\",\n21:     \"ruff>=0.7.2\",\n22: ]\n23: \n24: [tool.ruff]\n25: target-version = \"py312\"\n26: \n27: [tool.ruff.lint]\n28: select = [\"ALL\"]\n29: ignore = [\"D\", \"COM812\", \"ISC001\", \"T201\", \"T203\", \"TRY003\", \"PLR2004\", \"EM\", \"G004\"]\n30: \n31: [tool.ruff.format]\n32: docstring-code-format = true\n33: \n34: [tool.pyright]\n35: pythonVersion = \"3.12\"\n36: typeCheckingMode = \"strict\""},"status":"done","trackFiles":["file:///Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/py/pyproject.toml"]},"toolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_01H9R1rMEaYrFTH5CUo2Sz1s","type":"tool_result"},{"run":{"result":[".gitignore",".python-version","README.md","data/","oidc_attestation_validation.py","pki_attestation_validation.py","pyproject.toml","uv.lock"],"status":"done"},"toolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_01NnqJPTQMzrafpGXbx53oV1","type":"tool_result"},{"run":{"result":["IAttestation.sol","IVerification.sol"],"status":"done"},"toolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_014t6eZAqMaVudYjFMK39xJf","type":"tool_result"},{"run":{"progress":{},"result":{"absolutePath":"/Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/contracts/FlareVtpmAttestation.sol","content":"1: // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n2: pragma solidity ^0.8.27;\n3: \n4: import {IAttestation} from \"./interfaces/IAttestation.sol\";\n5: import {IVerification} from \"./interfaces/IVerification.sol\";\n6: import {BaseQuoteConfig, Header, QuoteConfig} from \"./types/Common.sol\";\n7: import {InvalidVerifier, PayloadValidationFailed, SignatureVerificationFailed} from \"./types/Common.sol\";\n8: import {ParserUtils} from \"./utils/ParserUtils.sol\";\n9: import {Ownable} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/access/Ownable.sol\";\n10: \n11: /**\n12:  * @title FlareVtpmAttestation\n13:  * @dev A contract for verifying RSA-signed JWTs and registering virtual Trusted Platform Module (vTPM) attestations.\n14:  * Allows for configuring required vTPM specifications and validating token-based attestations.\n15:  */\n16: contract FlareVtpmAttestation is IAttestation, Ownable {\n17:     /// @notice Stores the vTPM configurations for each registered address\n18:     mapping(address => QuoteConfig) public registeredQuotes;\n19: \n20:     /// @notice Event emitted when a new vTPM quote configuration is registered\n21:     event QuoteRegistered(address indexed sender, QuoteConfig config);\n22: \n23:     /// @notice Event emitted when the base vTPM configuration requirements are updated\n24:     event BaseQuoteConfigUpdated(string indexed imageDigest, string hwmodel, string swname, string iss, bool secboot);\n25: \n26:     /// @notice The required base configuration for a vTPM to be considered valid\n27:     BaseQuoteConfig internal requiredConfig;\n28: \n29:     /// @notice Mapping of token types to their respective verifier contracts\n30:     mapping(bytes => IVerification) public tokenTypeVerifiers;\n31: \n32:     /**\n33:      * @dev Initializes the contract, setting the deployer as the initial owner.\n34:      */\n35:     constructor() Ownable(msg.sender) {}\n36: \n37:     /**\n38:      * @dev Assigns a verifier contract to handle a specific token type.\n39:      * @param verifier Address of the contract implementing the IVerification interface for this token type.\n40:      */\n41:     function setTokenTypeVerifier(address verifier) external onlyOwner {\n42:         IVerification tokenTypeVerifier = IVerification(verifier);\n43:         bytes memory tokenType = tokenTypeVerifier.tokenType();\n44:         if (tokenType.length == 0) {\n45:             revert InvalidVerifier();\n46:         }\n47:         tokenTypeVerifiers[tokenType] = tokenTypeVerifier;\n48:     }\n49: \n50:     /**\n[... omitted lines 51 to ∞ ...]"},"status":"done","trackFiles":["file:///Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/contracts/FlareVtpmAttestation.sol"]},"toolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_01Af8RAvA83Vjd1kQZeRXzgZ","type":"tool_result"},{"run":{"progress":{},"result":{"absolutePath":"/Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/test/FlareVtpmAttestation.t.sol","content":"1: // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n2: pragma solidity ^0.8.27;\n3: \n4: import {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n5: import {console} from \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n6: \n7: import {FlareVtpmAttestation} from \"../contracts/FlareVtpmAttestation.sol\";\n8: import {OidcSignatureVerification} from \"../contracts/verifiers/OidcSignatureVerification.sol\";\n9: \n10: import {\n11:     Header, PayloadValidationFailed, QuoteConfig, SignatureVerificationFailed\n12: } from \"../contracts/types/Common.sol\";\n13: \n14: /**\n15:  * @title FlareVtpmAttestationTest\n16:  * @dev Test suite for the FlareVtpmAttestation contract.\n17:  */\n18: contract FlareVtpmAttestationTest is Test {\n19:     /// @notice Instance of the contract to be tested\n20:     FlareVtpmAttestation public flareVtpm;\n21:     OidcSignatureVerification public oidcVerifier;\n22: \n23:     // Example attestation token components for testing (Base64URL decoded)\n24:     bytes constant HEADER =\n25:         hex\"7b22616c67223a225253323536222c226b6964223a2234363736633439306463343338323936333635393534343265393363646335643237616161323739222c22747970223a224a5754227d\";\n26:     bytes constant PAYLOAD =\n27:         hex\"\";\n28: \n29:     bytes constant SIGNATURE =\n30:         hex\"\";\n[... omitted lines 31 to ∞ ...]"},"status":"done","trackFiles":["file:///Users/ofux/work/agentic/flare-vtpm-attestation/test/FlareVtpmAttestation.t.sol"]},"toolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_01B4EwGghiuQazcQWYtZFuYA","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},{"content":[],"role":"assistant","state":{"type":"streaming"}}],"title":"Create comprehensive agent documentation file","v":186,"~debug":{"lastInferenceInput":{"max_tokens":32000,"messages":[{"content":[{"text":"Please analyze this codebase and create an AGENT.md file containing:\n1. Build/lint/test commands - especially for running a single test\n2. Architecture and codebase structure information, including important subprojects, internal APIs, databases, etc.\n3. Code style guidelines, including imports, conventions, formatting, types, naming conventions, error handling, etc.\n\nThe file you create will be given to agentic coding tools (such as yourself) that operate in this repository. Make it about 20 lines long.\n\nIf there are Cursor rules (in .cursor/rules/ or .cursorrules), Claude rules (CLAUDE.md), Windsurf rules (.windsurfrules), Cline rules (.clinerules), Goose rules (.goosehints), or Copilot rules (in .github/copilot-instructions.md), make sure to include them. Also, first check if there is a AGENT.md file, and if